  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening Migration Management System for Enhanced Border Security in Rwanda</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Rwanda continues to face security risks due to the proximity to volatile security contexts within neighbouring countries where armed groups are active, particularly at the border with the Democratic Republic of The Congo (DRC).  The security risks may impact adversely both national security as well as measures and programs aiming to provide a safe refuge to migrants and refugees within Rwanda. Therefore, providing a safe route through international airports and land borders in Rwanda is critical to maintain the standards of security and the possibility for Rwanda to support migrants and refugees in need as well as to play its critical role in the continental trade and free movement of people. Against this backdrop, the project aims to enhance border security in Rwanda main points of entry and protect vulnerable travellers and migrants, by strengthening its security system and equipment at the Kigali International Airport and Poids Lourds Border Post and the capacity of population and officers at the borders.</narrative>
  </description>
